-- Step 30: stock transfers, stock adjustments (and opening stock), and stock counts.
-- track: B
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with drizzle/down/0020_stock_documents.sql.
--
-- Three kinds of document move stock by hand. Each is a draft that the app writes, and is
-- posted once, by a function of the database's own, which takes the number, writes the stock
-- moves through app.move_stock (drizzle/0017_delivery_notes.sql, unchanged) and, where the
-- value of stock changes, posts the journal:
--
--   a transfer        goods leave one warehouse at its weighted-average cost and arrive in the
--                     other worth exactly that; the books do not change, so no journal;
--   an adjustment     goods taken out at the weighted-average cost, or added at a stated cost:
--                     stock against the stock adjustments account (5110); as opening stock,
--                     against opening balance equity (3900);
--   a count           the difference between what was counted and what the books held, line by
--                     line, the same way: stock against the stock adjustments account.
--
-- The app's role cannot write a document's status, its number, who posted it or its journal:
-- it has no right to those columns. It cannot write a stock move or a journal of these kinds
-- at all. A posted document and its lines never change; a wrong one is put right by an
-- opposite document, which is valued as any other at the cost of the day.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE200 to SE299 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE200  no such document in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE201  the document is not in the state this needs (only a draft is posted, and so on)
--   SE202  nothing to post: no lines, or nothing counted
--   SE203  a finished or posted stock document is never changed or removed
--   SE204  a line is written only while its document is a draft
--   SE205  goods coming in need a cost, and none is stated or known
--   SE206  stock has moved since the count sheet was started
--   SE207  stock documents are posted in read committed transactions
--   SE208  a transfer between the warehouses of two branches is not available yet
--   SE209  the document changed after whoever is posting it last looked at it
--   SE210  opening stock is dated on the day the books opened

